  "faqTickets": "Where are my tickets?",
  "faqTicketsBody": "Open My Tickets after confirming checkout. Each issued ticket has its own QR. You can share a PDF from its ticket card.",
  "faqRefundBody": "Refund rules are shown on the event page. Contact support with your order details before requesting a refund.",
  "faqCheckin": "How do I enter the event?",
  "faqCheckinBody": "Show the full ticket QR at the entrance. If scanning fails, show the signed credential to staff. A ticket admits once unless staff reverse the check-in.",
  "policyUnavailable": "No published policy has been provided in this app. Contact support for the current official document.",
  "faqAttendeeTitle": "Attendee FAQ",
  "faqOrganizerTitle": "Organizer FAQ",
  "faqAttendeeBooking": "How do I book tickets and use a promo code?",
  "faqAttendeeBookingBody": "Open an event, choose ticket types and quantities, and enter a promo code if you have one. Continue to checkout, enter attendee details, and review the final discount, fees and total before confirming. Complete checkout before the reservation timer expires.",
  "faqAttendeePayment": "Will I be charged real money?",
  "faqAttendeePaymentBody": "Payments currently run in demo mode. No real money is charged. Confirming a successful booking still issues real admission tickets that can be checked in.",
  "faqAttendeeOrganizerBody": "Open Profile → Become an organizer. Submit your contact name, organization, phone and event plans. Wait for admin approval, refresh the application status, then open the organizer dashboard once approved.",
  "faqOrganizerPublish": "How do I create and publish an event?",
  "faqOrganizerPublishBody": "Open My Events → Create event. Enter the title, venue, city, street address, date, category, description and ticket price, then publish. The current mobile form creates 100 General admission tickets and uses 18:00–22:00. If publishing fails after the draft is saved, refresh My Events and check the saved draft before creating another event.",
  "faqOrganizerPaid": "Why are paid ticket sales unavailable?",
  "faqOrganizerPaidBody": "Organizer application approval grants organizer access only. Paid sales additionally require backend identity verification, a connected and verified payout account, the activation fee and accepted terms. These checks are separate from the Become an organizer application and cannot all be completed in the current mobile form.",
  "faqOrganizerStaff": "How do I assign event staff?",
  "faqOrganizerStaffBody": "Open My Events, select an event and tap Assign staff. Enter the email of an existing registered user. The backend assigns that user to this event. Ask them to sign out and sign in again to open the staff screen and see their assigned events.",
  "faqOrganizerCheckin": "How do I check in attendees?",
  "faqOrganizerCheckinBody": "Open Check-in and select the correct event, or open Check-in from its event page. Scan the ticket QR or paste the full signed credential if scanning is unavailable. The backend rejects invalid, wrong-event, cancelled, refunded and already-used tickets. Camera scanning needs camera permission and should be tested on a physical phone.",
  "faqOrganizerSales": "Where can I see sales and registrations?",
  "faqOrganizerSalesBody": "Use the organizer dashboard for totals. Open an event for its ticket sales, capacity and revenue, then View attendees for confirmed registrations. Revenue is calculated from confirmed orders, including their fees and discounts; pending and failed orders are not counted as confirmed revenue.",
  "faqOrganizerSupport": "How do I respond to attendee support requests?",
  "faqOrganizerSupportBody": "Open Profile → Contact us to view support cases available to your account, including those linked to events you own. Open a case to read its messages and send a reply. Refresh the list or conversation to load updates.",
  "categoryOther": "Other"
